	 * - Bridged the checker’s ADD decode (chk.spec_valid) to PicoRV32 internal decode,
	 *   using 1-cycle delayed flags (prev_instr_add/prev_instr_trap) since RVFI/checker
	 *   observes the retiring instruction later than the internal decode flags.
	 * - Added “knownness” helpers for selected RVFI fields when (check && rvfi_valid)
	 *   using reduction-x checks (important because SVA treats X as failure).
	 * - Added an rd writeback alignment helper for the *writeback case* using 1-cycle
	 *   shadow regs: if last cycle had a non-IRQ cpuregs_write, then current RVFI rd_*
	 *   must reflect that write.
	 *
	 * What remains hard:
	 * - o_rd_wdata_match still generate hard transitions.
	 *   The remaining traces tend to underconstrain the PC/writeback datapaths,
	 *   so IC3 can’t easily rule out “spec_valid true but PC/rd update mismatched”.
	 *
	 * Future directions (next iteration ideas):
	 * - Strengthen the bridge around chk.spec_valid to include additional internal
	 *   state that must coincide with an ADD retirement (e.g. cpu_state sequencing
	 *   around fetch/ld_rs/exec and decoder_trigger/mem_done timing), but without
	 *   directly re-asserting o_*.
	 * - For RD: further split cases (x0 write suppressed, IRQ/QREGS paths, etc.) and
	 *   add only one-way implications from concrete microarchitectural events.
